    "resolved_from_fallback": true,
    "final_cot": "First describe the image: The figure shows citrus A (diploid) obtaining citrus A haploid through “anther (pollen) in vitro culture”, and then obtaining “protoplast of citrus A haploid” through process ①; citrus B (diploid) obtains “protoplast of citrus B diploid” through process ①. The two kinds of protoplasts converge at process ② to form a “hybrid cell”, and then form a “triploid plant” through process ③. Then reason: Process ② corresponds to the fusion of two protoplasts. When protoplasts fuse, the cell membranes need to contact and fuse with each other, which depends on biological membranes having a certain fluidity. Therefore, the realization of process ② depends on membrane fluidity.",
